	<group name="Encryption Tool">
		<!-- the mod pack / script encryption tool: tabs, buttons, status line, help page -->
		<str id="encTool.dialog.choosePacks">Choose the mod pack(s) (.zip) to encrypt</str>
		<str id="encTool.dialog.chooseProtected">Choose the protected script(s) (.hxb)</str>
		<str id="encTool.dialog.chooseScripts">Choose the script(s) to protect</str>
		<str id="encTool.dialog.saveKey">Save the script key as script_key.txt</str>
		<str id="encTool.error.alreadyEncrypted">That file is already an encrypted (CNEZ) mod pack: {0}</str>
		<str id="encTool.error.alreadyPassword">That zip is already password protected. Remove its password first, the exporter needs a plain zip.</str>
		<str id="encTool.error.notZip">That file is not a zip archive: {0}</str>
		<str id="encTool.error.unreadable">Cannot read {0}: {1}</str>
		<str id="encTool.help.body">WHAT THIS TOOL DOES\n\nThe Mod Pack tab seals a zip mod into a CNEZ container or an AES-256 password zip, unwraps\neither one into a plain zip again, and turns keys into shareable tokens. The Scripts tab\nseals a single script into a .hxb the engine keeps loading like a .hx.\n\nkeys\n\nThe key is whatever sits in the Key field of the token tool. Empty means: the key\nscript_key.txt (next to the executable or in the mod folder) has for that pack name, or the\nbuilt-in engine key. A custom key must also be in script_key.txt, or the engine cannot open\nthe pack again. File &gt; Reload Key File re-reads it without a restart. script_key.txt holds\neither one key on its first line, or one "name = key" per line, where name is a file name,\na name without extension, a mod relative path, or * as fallback; # and // start a comment.\n\nkey tokens: a token (CNEK1-...) is the key rewritten as different text. Players paste it\ninto the prompt that opens an encrypted zip mod. Copy Key / Copy Token put either one on\nthe clipboard.\n\nmod pack formats\n\n  CNEZ container: only the engine can open it, the key is required.\n  AES-256 zip: 7-Zip, WinRAR and Bandizip open it with the password, and so does the\n  engine, so players only type the password once.\n\nthe Scripts tab\n\nPick one or more .hx files, pick a protection mode, switch on any extra layer you want and\nit writes name_protected.hxb next to the source. The engine loads .hxb like any other\nscript, so the .hx can be deleted afterwards and the protected file takes its place.\n\n  protection mode - required, exactly one of the two:\n  key encryption: ChaCha20 plus an HMAC tag, the same key rules as above. The payload\n  is the source, so Decrypt can turn the file back into .hx.\n  VM bytecode: compiled with a per file random opcode permutation, so a disassembly of\n  one script does not describe the next. Compiling drops the source text, so the file\n  runs but Decrypt has nothing to write out.\n\n  extra layers - optional, they stack on the mode above:\n  byte offset: the payload is rotated by N bits, which stops a plain file signature.\n  split: the payload is cut into pieces, shuffled, with random padding in between.\n  Both are pure byte shuffles: the numbers needed to undo them sit in the plain header,\n  so they never keep a file from being restored.\n\nWhy a mode and not both: the source copy is only ever embedded when it is encrypted as\nwell (an unencrypted copy would be readable straight out of the file), and a VM pack has\nno key to seal it with. So: key mode is the restorable one, VM mode is the one that only\nthe game can read.\n\nEncrypting and decrypting both run in the background with a progress bar and write a new\nfile next to the source: name_encrypted.zip, name_password.zip or name_decrypted.zip.\nPlain zips load as before; password zips from other tools load too (ZipCrypto, AES-128/192/\n256) - the password is asked at startup and the readable copy stays in the hidden\n.cne/keys folder, which is deleted when the game closes.\n\ntips: while a text field is focused Backspace edits it and ESC only drops the focus, ESC\nagain leaves the editor. The mouse wheel scrolls this page.\n</str>
		<str id="encTool.help.scrollHint">Help - scroll the text with the mouse wheel.</str>
		<str id="encTool.help.title">Help &amp; About</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.help">About / Help</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.integrity">Generate integrity manifest</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.modPack">Mod Pack tab</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.reloadKey">Reload Key File (script_key.txt)</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.scripts">Scripts tab</str>
		<str id="encTool.menu.selfTest">Self test: containers (scripts + mod packs)</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.chooseDecrypt">Choose encrypted .zip and Decrypt...</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.chooseEncrypt">Choose .zip and Encrypt...</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.descStandard">Standard: the zip stays a normal zip, but every entry is encrypted with AES-256 (WinZip AES).\n7-Zip, WinRAR and Bandizip open it with the password, and so does the engine - players are asked\nfor that password at startup. Hand out the key or a token: the same password works in both.</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.descStrong">Enhanced: the zip is wrapped in a CNEZ container. No archive tool can open it at all - only\nCodename Engine can, with the key (or a token). Safest option, but nobody can browse the mod in\n7-Zip and every tool that expects a real zip just sees garbage.</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.modeStandard">Standard: password zip (AES-256)</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.modeStrong">Enhanced: CNE container (CNEZ, needs the key)</str>
		<str id="encTool.pack.title">Encrypt a zip mod pack</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.chooseDecrypt">Choose .hxb and Decrypt...</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.chooseEncrypt">Choose .hx scripts and Encrypt...</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.extraTitle">Extra layers - optional, they stack on the mode above:</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.intro">Pick one protection mode first - it is required, exactly one of the two. The engine reads .hxb\ntransparently, so a protected script is a drop in replacement for the .hx it came from - same name,\ndifferent extension. Key mode also keeps a copy of the source, so Decrypt can turn the file back\ninto .hx. VM mode only stores bytecode, so the game runs it but Decrypt has nothing to write out.</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.modeKey">Key encryption - ChaCha20 + HMAC tag, needs the key (source can be restored)</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.modeKeyShort">key</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.modeTitle">Protection mode - pick one (required):</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.modeVM">VM bytecode - compiled, with a per file opcode permutation (bytecode only)</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.modeVMShort">VM bytecode</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.noExtra">no extra layer</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.offset">Byte offset - the whole payload rotated by N bits</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.offsetBits">Offset bits (1-16):</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.password">Password:</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.restoreKey">The source travels inside the file, so Decrypt can restore it.</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.restoreVM">Bytecode only, so Decrypt cannot write the source back out.</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.saveKey">Save Key File...</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.split">Split - cut into pieces, shuffled, padding in between</str>
		<str id="encTool.script.splitPieces">Split pieces (2-16):</str>
